  "interpretation": "Original add_bcd_and_draw_amiga_digits stores D0 to source scratch, forms app720 as one-past the existing canonical four-byte player_score_bcd owner71C..720, then three ABCD source/destination predecrements modify score bytes71F,71E,71D. Subsequent LONG read at resultingA1-1 reloads whole71C..720. High score byte71C is not changed by this three-byte addition. Original six-glyph path remains; ordinary ADD.W award producers do not establish valid packedBCD for every input. Shared decoded predecrement operands use independent An values; distinct source/destination registers can update independently even if cells alias. Same-register paired update remains conservatively refused. Existing A6 fallback facts stay conditional, no new app-base seed or object bound. Preserve carry/extend chains, original byte order, data and runtime behavior; no injected gameplay, repaired score arithmetic or new all-path claim.",
  "cause": [
    "The derived app-span helper blanket-refused any other predecrement operand, even with a distinct EA register. Original score/periodic routines therefore lost their app cursor at their first ABCD.",
    "A paired known-cursor regression then showed only the final auto-updated An survived. The transfer kept one pending cursor value. Two operand refs were recorded but the source cursor was lost afterward."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Share the existing per-operand pre/postincrement check: distinct EA registers update independently, while repeated use of the same An is still refused. No opcode/address recognizer or parallel transfer semantics.",
    "Keep up to four operand updates locally for one instruction, snapshotting the incoming cursor values before the ordinary decoded register-write invalidation. Restore every qualified independent updated cursor. No extra per-CFG-node arrays or new value domain.",
    "Two canonical comments explain the original low-three-byte score carry chain and one-past address. No generated-source edits, new names guessed from constants, changed game bytes or base-seeding shortcuts."
  ],
  "reproducer": {
    "initial_paired_suite": "7 positive failures /3 conservative passes before the change; recorded /tmp/sg2-paired-predec-before-tests.log and /tmp/sg2-paired-predec-before.json privately",
    "intermediate": "Removing the blanket refusal alone left one failure: with two aliased-cell independent An cursors, both ABCD operands were recorded but only the last An survived. Expected4 refs, observed3. The transfer correction retains both.",
    "coverage": "ABCD/SBCD, ADDX/SUBX WORD/LONG, CMPM byte/word/long, two distinct registers pointing at the same cell, same-register repeated update refusal, clobbers and unowned weak bases, plus existing transfer/stack/join/counter/catalogue guards."
  },
